  "description": "The Steiner tree problem in graphs track of FrontierCO (Feng et al., 2025), 88 instances in the SteinLib STP format: 23 easy test instances (the G instances, each the presolved reduction of a larger original whose fixed value, bounds and original counts the instance's meta carries), 50 hard test instances from SteinLib's bipartite (bip), code covering (cc) and hypercube (hc) sets, and 15 validation instances (generated hypercube graphs and GeoSteiner's reduced full Steiner tree graphs of random points, R25K). In each, the nodes are 1 to n, those that must be connected of type terminal and the rest of type node, and every edge is undirected with its weight; the Comment section's name, creator and remark are in the meta. FrontierCO's reference value for each instance is in the track's config.py.",
  "domain": "Steiner tree problem in graphs",
  "expectedCounts": {
    "instances": 88
  },
